WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.637
What does Oracle leave to you?

2
00:00:01.637 --> 00:00:05.888
Updates to one announcement form
a chain, so a rescheduled window

3
00:00:05.888 --> 00:00:10.375
arrives as a new announcement; read
every one and you keep the old date.

4
00:00:10.375 --> 00:00:13.437
Several announcement types
mean the same kind of news.

5
00:00:13.437 --> 00:00:16.147
The window and the deadline sit in generic

6
00:00:16.147 --> 00:00:19.088
time fields whose meaning
is in another field.

7
00:00:19.088 --> 00:00:22.424
The affected resources come
only from the details call.

8
00:00:22.424 --> 00:00:25.737
Oracle's reference doesn't
show the CLI's key casing.

9
00:00:25.737 --> 00:00:27.250
And the realms need a guard.

10
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.275
Each gap is pinned by a test.

11
00:00:29.275 --> 00:00:32.990
The verdict: use Oracle's
commands and policy as published,

12
00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:36.600
and build the chains, the time
fields and the realm guard.
